      "writtenOn": "2018-02-08T18:29:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "As an aside, I think we need that change that Shawn was working on.\n\nFor the current issue where we send the SoftReset with the wrong role bit, I think we could save our data role as well. Basically, turn the battery backed byte in RAM to a byte of flags. Maybe bit 0 means explicit contract in place, bit 1 could be data role. We could also expand upon this if we needed to keep more state. This should be applicable for EC soft resets (e.g. reboot, sysjump).\n\nIf it\u0027s a hard reset or no explicit contract in place, we should set the data roles to their default for Source vs Sink.\n\nThoughts? I may give this a try today.",
      "parentUuid": "c737e94a_1784589f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 21,
